{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The War Within and City of Evil feel like natural next choices because their aggressive riffs and melodic heaviness connect with what I enjoyed in In Flames and Soilwork.",
    "Believe gives me a clear way to explore more Disturbed after Ten Thousand Fists, while Mezmerize appeals to my current interest in forceful riffs and unusual rhythms."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Fallen feels off for this visit because its softer, atmospheric sound does not satisfy my current desire for riff-driven metal.",
    "Us and Them and Gasoline fit my broader listening history, but melodic hard rock is less compelling to me right now than the heavier choices."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My past interest in melodic rock seems to carry too much weight when I am currently looking for heavier music.",
    "Several albums share a heavy sound, but that alone does not make me want to choose all of them now; I would start with City of Evil before Waking the Fallen and The War Within before Curse."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest listening to Ten Thousand Fists and 10.000 Days makes heavy riffs and rhythmic complexity especially appealing this visit.",
    "An album can fit my taste without being an immediate choice; I am selective and would prioritize a few strong matches before exploring the others."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in heavy, melodic music but give my broader rock tastes more weight than my current preference for aggressive riffs and engaging rhythms."
}"}
